(LSTM Variants for Chaotic Dynamical Systems: An Empirical Study on the Lorenz Attractor) Tj
T*
(Ruslan Gokhman - Yeshiva University - rgokhman@mail.yu.edu) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(Forecasting chaotic dynamical systems such as the Lorenz attractor is notoriously difficult:) Tj
T*
(small numerical errors are amplified exponentially over long autoregressive rollouts.) Tj
T*
(We study seven recurrent and convolutional architectures for the AI-DEEDS 2026) Tj
T*
(Chaotic Systems Challenge: a vanilla LSTM, an LSTM with additive attention,) Tj
T*
(a Bidirectional LSTM \(BiLSTM\), a BiLSTM trained with the Huber loss,) Tj
T*
(a Temporal Convolutional Network \(TCN\), a CNN front-end followed by an LSTM,) Tj
T*
(and a CNN front-end followed by a BiLSTM. All models share the same pre-processing,) Tj
T*
(sequence length, and rollout procedure, isolating the contribution of each design choice.) Tj
T*
(The challenge scores predictions on a 0-100 scale where higher is better.) Tj
T*
(We obtain leaderboard scores between 45.72 and 58.81, with the BiLSTM trained) Tj
T*
(with Huber loss being the strongest configuration.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Keywords: Chaotic systems, Lorenz attractor, LSTM, BiLSTM, Huber loss, time-series forecasting) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1 Introduction) Tj
T*
(The Lorenz 63 system is a canonical example of deterministic chaos: a three-dimensional) Tj
T*
(ODE whose trajectories never repeat and depend sensitively on initial conditions.) Tj
T*
(Tiny errors in the predicted state are amplified exponentially by the positive Lyapunov exponent.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2 Related Work) Tj
T*
(Common Task Frameworks for scientific ML. The AI-DEEDS competition is part of a growing) Tj
T*
(family of Common Task Frameworks \(CTFs\) designed to replace ad hoc comparisons.) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
